// 5-level nesting: edges that cross several group walls, siblings and cousins.
title Deep nesting
direction right

Client [icon: monitor]
Partner [icon: globe]

Cloud [icon: cloud] {
	Edge [icon: shield] {
		CDN [icon: zap]
		WAF [icon: shield-check]
	}
	Region [icon: map] {
		VPC [icon: network] {
			Public subnet {
				LB [icon: server]
				NAT [icon: router]
			}
			Private subnet {
				Cluster [icon: box] {
					API [icon: server]
					Worker [icon: cpu]
					Scheduler [icon: clock]
				}
				Cache [icon: zap]
			}
			Data subnet {
				Primary DB [icon: database, shape: cylinder]
				Replica DB [icon: database, shape: cylinder]
			}
		}
		Queue [icon: radio]
	}
	Observability {
		Logs [icon: file-text]
		Metrics [icon: activity]
	}
}

Client > CDN: HTTPS
Partner > WAF
CDN > WAF > LB
LB > API
API > Worker
API > Cache
Worker > Queue: jobs
Scheduler > Worker
Queue > Worker
API > Primary DB: writes
Primary DB > Replica DB: replication
Worker > Replica DB: reads
API --> Logs
Worker --> Metrics
NAT > Partner
Cluster --> Metrics: health
